**When.** Section 7A requires CDD when the bank:

- enters a business relationship;
- carries out an occasional transaction (SBP requires CDD for **every** occasional customer);
- suspects money laundering or terrorist financing; or
- doubts the accuracy or adequacy of data it already holds.

**What.** The bank must:

- identify the customer and verify identity from reliable, independent sources, checking with the issuing source such as NADRA where possible;
- identify the **beneficial owner** and take reasonable steps to verify who it is;
- understand the purpose and intended nature of the relationship; and
- **monitor** the relationship on an ongoing basis.

**Never.** No anonymous or fictitious-name relationships (section 7E), no numbered accounts, and no personal accounts used for business beyond the narrow exceptions. Anyone acting for a customer must be identified and verified, and so must their authority to act.
